        <p class="lead">Everything you need to know about models, applications, cutting depths and hire options — answered directly from the factory in Lingen.</p>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="faq-list reveal">

      <details class="faq-item">
        <summary>How deep can a trench cutter cut?<span class="faq-icon"><svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2"><path d="M12 5v14M5 12h14"/></svg></span></summary>
        <p class="faq-answer">Cutting depth depends on the model. Compact excavator-mounted cutters (GM 140 H) reach up to 900 mm. Tractor-mounted models such as the GM 180 AF cut to 1,800 mm. Deep-cut machines such as the GM 300 HF and GM 450 H enable work to depths of 3,000 mm — for demanding special civil engineering and district heating projects.</p>
      </details>

      <details class="faq-item">
        <summary>Which trench cutters are available for excavator attachment?<span class="faq-icon"><svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2"><path d="M12 5v14M5 12h14"/></svg></span></summary>
        <p class="faq-answer">LIBA offers the following trench cutters as excavator attachments: GM 140 H (from 6 t, up to 900 mm cutting depth), GM 140 AFH-500 (up to 500 mm, from 8 t) and GM 140 AFH-600 (up to 600 mm, from 12 t). These attachment cutters are hydraulically driven via the excavator hydraulics and are quick-coupler compatible.</p>
      </details>

      <details class="faq-item">
        <summary>Which trench cutters are suitable for tractors?<span class="faq-icon"><svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2"><path d="M12 5v14M5 12h14"/></svg></span></summary>
        <p class="faq-answer">Suitable tractor-mounted trench cutters include: GM 1 AF, GM 1 AS (up to 400 mm, compact), GM 140 AF, GM 160 AF, GM 160 AS (up to 1,200 mm, mid-range) and GM 180 AF and GM 600 R (up to 1,800 mm, high-performance). Model selection depends on cutting depth, cutting width and the available carrier machine.</p>
      </details>

      <details class="faq-item">
        <summary>Can a trench cutter be used in hard ground or rock?<span class="faq-icon"><svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2"><path d="M12 5v14M5 12h14"/></svg></span></summary>
        <p class="faq-answer">Yes. The self-propelled GM 6 ASR trench cutter was developed specifically for hard rock up to rock class IV. It performs reliably in limestone, slate and mining environments, reaching cutting depths of up to 800 mm in rock — economically viable where excavators and cut-off saws are not profitable.</p>
      </details>

      <details class="faq-item">
        <summary>Can I hire a trench cutter from Lingener Baumaschinen?<span class="faq-icon"><svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2"><path d="M12 5v14M5 12h14"/></svg></span></summary>
        <p class="faq-answer">Yes. LIBA offers trench cutters for daily, weekly and monthly hire. Available models are GM 4 All-Wheel, GM 4 Crawler and GM 6 ASR — each with operator training and 24/7 factory hotline during deployment. Up to 100% of hire costs can be offset against a subsequent purchase. <a href="/en/mieten.html" style="color:var(--brand);text-decoration:underline;">Go to hire page</a></p>
      </details>

      <details class="faq-item">
        <summary>Are used trench cutters available?<span class="faq-icon"><svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2"><path d="M12 5v14M5 12h14"/></svg></span></summary>
        <p class="faq-answer">Yes. LIBA sells used trench cutters directly from the factory — after a full factory inspection, with a complete machine history and warranty on all parts replaced during inspection. No middlemen, no premium. <a href="/en/gebrauchtmaschinen.html" style="color:var(--brand);text-decoration:underline;">View used machines</a></p>
      </details>

      <details class="faq-item">
        <summary>In which countries are LIBA trench cutters available?<span class="faq-icon"><svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2"><path d="M12 5v14M5 12h14"/></svg></span></summary>
        <p class="faq-answer">Lingener Baumaschinen has been operating since 1969 and delivers trench cutters to over 60 countries worldwide. Sales and delivery are made direct from the Lingen (Ems) factory — including low-loader transport on request. For international enquiries and dealer information, please contact <a href="/en/kontakt.html" style="color:var(--brand);text-decoration:underline;">info@lingener-baumaschinen.de</a> directly.</p>
      </details>

    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="section section-dark" id="kalkulator">
  <div class="container">
    <div class="section-header reveal">
      <div class="heading">
        <span class="section-index is-dark" style="color: var(--brand-light);">07 / Calculator</span>
        <h2 class="mt-3">How many metres of<br><em class="serif-italic">route can you achieve per day?</em></h2>
      </div>
      <div class="aside">
        <p class="lead">Indicative figures based on ground type and machine model. Exact values depend on configuration, operator profile and route geometry — please contact us.</p>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="reveal" style="background: rgba(255,255,255,.04); border: 1px solid rgba(255,255,255,.08); border-radius: var(--radius-lg, 16px); padding: clamp(1.5rem, 4vw, 2.5rem); max-width: 720px;">
      <div class="grid grid-2" style="gap: 1.5rem; margin-bottom: 1.5rem;">
        <div class="field">
          <label for="k-boden" style="color: var(--canvas); font-weight: 500;">Ground type</label>
          <select id="k-boden" style="margin-top: .5rem; background: var(--steel-900); color: var(--canvas); border-color: rgba(255,255,255,.12);">
            <option value="1000">Sand / loose ground</option>
            <option value="700" selected>Loamy ground</option>
            <option value="400">Compact clay / marl</option>
            <option value="200">Semi-rock / soft stone</option>
            <option value="80">Hard rock</option>
          </select>
        </div>
        <div class="field">
          <label for="k-modell" style="color: var(--canvas); font-weight: 500;">Machine model</label>
          <select id="k-modell" style="margin-top: .5rem; background: var(--steel-900); color: var(--canvas); border-color: rgba(255,255,255,.12);">
            <option value="1.0">GM 4 Crawler / All-Wheel</option>
            <option value="0.8">GM 180 AF (tractor-mounted)</option>
            <option value="0.6">GM 140 AFH (excavator attachment)</option>
            <option value="0.5">GM 450 H (deep-cut)</option>
            <option value="0.15">GM 6 ASR (rock cutter)</option>
          </select>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div id="k-result" style="border-top: 1px solid rgba(255,255,255,.1); padding-top: 1.5rem; display: grid; grid-template-columns: 1fr 1fr 1fr; gap: 1.25rem; text-align: center;">
        <div>
          <div style="font-family: var(--font-display); font-size: clamp(2rem, 5vw, 3rem); font-weight: 400; color: var(--brand-light); letter-spacing: -.04em;" id="k-day">0</div>
          <div style="font-size: .8rem; text-transform: uppercase; letter-spacing: .08em; color: var(--steel-400); margin-top: .25rem;">Metres / Day</div>
          <div style="margin-top: .85rem; height: 4px; background: rgba(255,255,255,.07); border-radius: 2px; overflow: hidden;">
            <div id="k-bar-day" style="height: 100%; width: 0%; background: linear-gradient(90deg, var(--brand), var(--brand-light)); border-radius: 2px; transition: width .65s cubic-bezier(.22,1,.36,1);"></div>
          </div>
        </div>
        <div>
          <div style="font-family: var(--font-display); font-size: clamp(2rem, 5vw, 3rem); font-weight: 400; color: var(--canvas); letter-spacing: -.04em;" id="k-week">0</div>
          <div style="font-size: .8rem; text-transform: uppercase; letter-spacing: .08em; color: var(--steel-400); margin-top: .25rem;">Metres / Week</div>
          <div style="margin-top: .85rem; height: 4px; background: rgba(255,255,255,.07); border-radius: 2px; overflow: hidden;">
            <div id="k-bar-week" style="height: 100%; width: 0%; background: rgba(255,255,255,.4); border-radius: 2px; transition: width .65s .08s cubic-bezier(.22,1,.36,1);"></div>
          </div>
        </div>
        <div>
          <div style="font-family: var(--font-display); font-size: clamp(2rem, 5vw, 3rem); font-weight: 400; color: var(--canvas); letter-spacing: -.04em;" id="k-month">0</div>
          <div style="font-size: .8rem; text-transform: uppercase; letter-spacing: .08em; color: var(--steel-400); margin-top: .25rem;">Metres / Month</div>
          <div style="margin-top: .85rem; height: 4px; background: rgba(255,255,255,.07); border-radius: 2px; overflow: hidden;">
            <div id="k-bar-month" style="height: 100%; width: 0%; background: rgba(255,255,255,.4); border-radius: 2px; transition: width .65s .16s cubic-bezier(.22,1,.36,1);"></div>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
      <p style="color: var(--steel-500); font-size: .8rem; margin-top: 1.25rem; font-family: var(--font-mono); letter-spacing: .02em;">Indicative figure · Variations of ±30% depending on configuration and operating conditions</p>
    </div>

    <script>
      (function(){
        var boden   = document.getElementById('k-boden');
        var modell  = document.getElementById('k-modell');
        var dayEl   = document.getElementById('k-day');
        var weekEl  = document.getElementById('k-week');
        var monthEl = document.getElementById('k-month');
        var barD    = document.getElementById('k-bar-day');
        var barW    = document.getElementById('k-bar-week');
        var barM    = document.getElementById('k-bar-month');
        var MAX     = 1000;
        var cur     = { d: 0, w: 0, m: 0 };
        var raf     = null;

        function calcDay() {
          var raw = parseInt(boden.value) * parseFloat(modell.value);
          if (raw >= 100) return Math.round(raw / 50) * 50;
          if (raw >= 20)  return Math.round(raw / 10) * 10;
          return Math.max(Math.round(raw / 5) * 5, 5);
        }

        function animateTo(target) {
          var from = { d: cur.d, w: cur.w, m: cur.m };
          var dur  = 650;
          var t0   = null;
          if (raf) cancelAnimationFrame(raf);
          (function step(ts) {
            if (!t0) t0 = ts;
            var p = Math.min((ts - t0) / dur, 1);
            var e = 1 - Math.pow(1 - p, 3);
            dayEl.textContent   = Math.round(from.d + (target.d - from.d) * e).toLocaleString('en');
            weekEl.textContent  = Math.round(from.w + (target.w - from.w) * e).toLocaleString('en');
            monthEl.textContent = Math.round(from.m + (target.m - from.m) * e).toLocaleString('en');
            if (p < 1) { raf = requestAnimationFrame(step); }
            else {
              dayEl.textContent   = target.d.toLocaleString('en');
              weekEl.textContent  = target.w.toLocaleString('en');
              monthEl.textContent = target.m.toLocaleString('en');
              cur = { d: target.d, w: target.w, m: target.m };
              raf = null;
            }
          })(performance.now());
          var pct = Math.max(target.d / MAX * 100, 2).toFixed(1);
          barD.style.width = pct + '%';
          barW.style.width = pct + '%';
          barM.style.width = pct + '%';
        }

        function update() { var d = calcDay(); animateTo({ d: d, w: d * 5, m: d * 20 }); }

        boden.addEventListener('change', update);
        modell.addEventListener('change', update);

        if ('IntersectionObserver' in window) {
          var io = new IntersectionObserver(function(entries) {
            if (entries[0].isIntersecting) { update(); io.disconnect(); }
          }, { threshold: 0.25 });
          io.observe(document.getElementById('kalkulator'));
        } else { update(); }
      })();
    </script>
  </div>
</section>

